      "writtenOn": "2021-12-17T00:50:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": " Hello, Thanks for your comment.\n \n As I already comment at uploading patch here, I also don\u0027t want to duplicate iommu_memory(GIC SFR) writing with vendor hook. But for Targeting multiple CPU irq action, we have no change (without changing mainstream).\n \n And for \"Targeting multiple CPUs for one IRQ\" (we call it \"Multi target IRQ\"), this is special case for Camera IRQ-reaction timing issue. From very old model, before 2014, we used that feature for fast IRQ reaction. Now, when we use GIC-600 HWIP, (gic-v3.c), we also using \"trace_android_rvh_gic_v3_set_affinity\" vendor hook to support targeting Multi CPU.\n  \n Anyway, I will also try to check affinity setting more. please wait and Thanks.",
      "revId": "5391b89f7b757f9cb53855d5d2416bfb49e9c900",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
