      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T02:05:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello, I\u0027ve checked for our camera device with GIC-400 using SOC.\n\nWe apply this patch and apply also set affinity to Little CPUs for our Camera irqs like below :\n207:        988        937        966       1032          0          0          0          0     GIC-0 428 Level     3a0-0-0\n208:        326        330        294        356          0          0          0          0     GIC-0 429 Level     3a0-1-1\n209:          0          0          0          0          0          0          0          0     GIC-0 248 Level     3a0-zsl-2\n210:        643        596        623        704          0          0          0          0     GIC-0 229 Level     3a0-strp-3\n\nAnd when I checked migrate irqs with ftrace, all required multi target irqs set for little CPUs like below: (I printed affinity value to passing \"irq_do_set_affinity\" function.)\n\n \u003c...\u003e-18      [001] d..2   127.549705: migrate_one_irq+0x108/0x1c0: [+][migration/1][migrate_one_irq,134] irq_number 207 to affinity 0xF\n \u003c...\u003e-18      [001] d..2   127.549712: migrate_one_irq+0x108/0x1c0: [+][migration/1][migrate_one_irq,134] irq_number 208 to affinity 0xF\n \u003c...\u003e-18      [001] d..2   127.549719: migrate_one_irq+0x108/0x1c0: [+][migration/1][migrate_one_irq,134] irq_number 209 to affinity 0xF\n \u003c...\u003e-18      [001] d..2   127.549728: migrate_one_irq+0x108/0x1c0: [+][migration/1][migrate_one_irq,134] irq_number 210 to affinity 0xF\n \nAs you know, this migration was happened when cpuhotplug out and it could go down to suspend without problem or warning messages.\n\nSo, I think we can use targeting multiple CPUs when we need fast reaction for specific drivers.",
